        }
      ],
      "text": "**Midterm: Weeks 1–5.** This is one of the three main study sections for the 40-minute October 29 midterm."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "8382f6eb-5782-5d99-b336-69c8e87c1ed0",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1,
          "chunk_id": "7aeba6d6-26bb-46de-a908-a730d2d2b619"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1,
          "chunk_id": "19639fbc-b928-40c9-90f8-84fe43e5f788"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1,
          "chunk_id": "80af8d17-712a-4141-bd67-73f2e43bbc96"
        }
      ],
      "level": 1,
      "text": "1. Place value and unsigned binary"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6a90ede9-c6e4-53ca-842e-17c1b233914e",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1,
          "chunk_id": "16b5beda-31b0-4447-a1ab-9ceeb8237f7d"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1,
          "chunk_id": "80af8d17-712a-4141-bd67-73f2e43bbc96"
        }
      ],
      "text": "A **bit** is one binary digit: 0 or 1. A bit pattern gets its numerical meaning from its base, bit width, and encoding.\n\n- **MSB:** the leftmost, highest-weight bit.\n- **LSB:** the rightmost, lowest-weight bit.\n- **Nibble:** 4 bits. **Byte:** 8 bits. These first examples are unsigned."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "657a6790-9777-5ffe-bdc3-81f5a875aeb9",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1,
          "chunk_id": "7aeba6d6-26bb-46de-a908-a730d2d2b619"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1,
          "chunk_id": "19639fbc-b928-40c9-90f8-84fe43e5f788"
        }
      ],
      "text": "In base $k$, every digit is between $0$ and $k-1$. Moving one position left multiplies its weight by $k$; moving right across the radix point divides by $k$."
    },
    {
      "type": "equation",
      "id": "f300eaf9-6422-5a28-90c4-8a4c5beb7798",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1,
          "chunk_id": "19639fbc-b928-40c9-90f8-84fe43e5f788"
        }
      ],
      "latex": "V=\\sum_{i=-m}^{n-1}b_i k^i"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "69a0011a-3618-5db5-aabc-ad99c0305d9d",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1,
          "chunk_id": "19639fbc-b928-40c9-90f8-84fe43e5f788"
        }
      ],
      "text": "$b_i$ is the digit at position $i$; $n$ digits lie before the radix point and $m$ after it. The units digit has index 0."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "id": "a3186ce8-7626-5570-9c42-8e963100333b",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1,
          "chunk_id": "19639fbc-b928-40c9-90f8-84fe43e5f788"
        }
      ],
      "columns": [
        "Position",
        "3",
        "2",
        "1",
        "0",
        "-1",
        "-2",
        "-3"
      ],
      "rows": [
